3	 *
4	 * AscendC DeepNorm — single_row strategy for all N sizes.
5	 * Fuses: x_add = x * alpha + gx → DeepNorm(x_add).
6	 * Supports float32 / float16 / bfloat16.
7	 *
8	 * Computation per row (all in float32 internally):
9	 *   1. x_add = x * alpha + gx
10	 *   2. mean = reduce_sum(x_add) / N
11	 *   3. diff = x_add - mean
12	 *   4. variance = reduce_sum(diff^2) / N + eps
13	 *   5. rstd = 1 / sqrt(variance)
14	 *   6. y_out = gamma * diff * rstd + beta
15	 *
16	 * Outputs: mean[M, 1], rstd[M, 1], y_out[M, N]
17	 *
18	 * UB budget (worst-case N=2048, float16):
19	 *   sB_:        4KB  (shared gamma/beta input)
20	 *   qX,qGX,qY: 12KB  (3 × N × sizeof(T))
21	 *   rB_:        8KB  (reduce scratch)
22	 *   sm_:       64B   (scalar sum)
23	 *   cA_:        8KB  (x cast)
24	 *   cB_:        8KB  (main compute: gx cast → diff^2 → gamma → beta)
25	 *   cD_:       32B   (scalar out buffer)
26	 *   Total:    ~40KB (well under 192KB UB)
27	 */
